{"slug":"gwen-moore","qid":"Q461698","name":"Gwen Moore","desc":"American politician (1951-)","article":"Gwen Moore","born":"1951-04-18","died":null,"birthplace":"Racine","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"WI-04","f":2005,"u":null},{"t":"State Senate of Wisconsin","w":"","f":1993,"u":2004},{"t":"Wisconsin State Assembly","w":"","f":1989,"u":1992}],"summary":"Gwendolynne Sophia Moore (born April 18, 1951) is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Wisconsin's 4th congressional district since 2005. A member of the Democratic Party, her district includes Milwaukee and several suburbs within Milwaukee County. Moore is the first woman to represent the 4th district as well as the second woman (after Tammy Baldwin) and the first African American elected to Congress from Wisconsin.","photo":{"f":"gwen-moore.jpg","by":"U.S. House Office of Photography/House Creative Services","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwen_Moore,_official_portrait,_116th_Congress.jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","n":"Gwen Moore","race":"WI-04"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":249938,"s":74.77,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":191955,"s":75.27,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":232668,"s":74.65,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":206487,"s":75.61,"w":true,"n":"Gwen S Moore"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":220181,"s":76.74,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":179045,"s":70.24,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":235257,"s":72.21,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":143559,"s":69.05,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":222728,"s":87.63,"w":true,"n":"Gwen Moore"},{"y":2006,"o":"H","k":"WI-04","p":"D","v":136735,"s":71.31,"w":tr